---
import DocLayout from "../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
---

<DocLayout
  title="Releases & licenses"
  eyebrow="SECTION 11 / DISTRIBUTION"
  description="Automated, reproducible releases deliver crates, Linux archives, checksums, and this manual."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Release channels</h2><table class="spec-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Channel</th><th>Artifact</th></tr></thead><tbody
        ><tr
          ><td>crates.io</td><td
            ><code>lanyard-ssh-agent</code> source package</td
          ></tr
        ><tr
          ><td>GitHub Releases</td><td
            >x86_64 and aarch64 Linux archives plus checksums</td
          ></tr
        ><tr
          ><td>Nix flake</td><td
            >package, app, checks, and Home Manager module</td
          ></tr
        ><tr><td>GitHub Pages</td><td>This versioned operator manual</td></tr
        ></tbody
      >
    </table>
    <h2>Versioning</h2><p>
      Release-plz derives changelog entries and versions from Conventional
      Commits. Cargo-dist builds platform artifacts. Reusable workflows are
      pinned to immutable revisions so changes to the release machinery are
      reviewable.
    </p>
    <h2>
      Verify a download
    </h2><pre><code>sha256sum --check lanyard-ssh-agent-*.sha256</code></pre>
    <h2>Dual license</h2><p>
      Unless explicitly stated otherwise, Lanyard is available under either the
      Apache License, Version 2.0 or the MIT license, at your option.
      Contributions are accepted under the same terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/jwilger/lanyard-ssh-agent/releases"
        >Browse releases →</a
      >
    </p>
  </div>
</DocLayout>
